printed FastK for fast.k = 1, 2, 2.9, 3, 3.5, 4, 0.5: 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 4, none
CHECK bb16.1 TRUE every fit prints a queue table after each step that adds terms, at degrees 1, 2 and 3 (1004 tables); its entries are exactly 1..T, T = terms so far
CHECK bb16.2 TRUE AgedRank = rank + fast.beta * (K - K_m) in all 12196 rows, rank = 0-based place by RssDelta largest first; fast.beta = 0 prints -1.0 in all 2298 of its rows
CHECK bb16.3 FALSE HYPOTHESIS equal AgedRank is ordered by entry number (holds in 690 of 1004 tables)
CHECK bb16.4 TRUE every table is sorted by AgedRank, equal AgedRank by rank (1505 tie groups, 593 where rank and entry order differ)
CHECK bb16.5 FALSE HYPOTHESIS equal RssDelta keeps the previous table's order (holds in 528 of 905 tables)
CHECK bb16.6 FALSE HYPOTHESIS equal RssDelta is ranked by entry number descending (holds in 59 of 1004 tables)
CHECK bb16.7 TRUE equal RssDelta is ranked by entry number ascending (1249 tie groups, 322 finite, e.g. 0 or -1; 448 where the previous order differs)
CHECK bb16.8 FALSE HYPOTHESIS age counts steps: AgedRank = rank + fast.beta * (K - K_m) / 2 (holds in 0 of 596 tables)
CHECK bb16.9 TRUE K = 2, 4, 6, ... in every fit, also after the 268 one-term steps; age is K - K_m, so fast.beta = 1 adds 2 per step
CHECK bb16.10 TRUE the next step visits the first max(3, trunc(fast.k)) rows in table order, all rows when trunc(fast.k) = 0 (970 steps)
CHECK bb16.11 TRUE fast.k = 1, 2, 2.9 and 3.5 print FastK 3 and fit as fast.k = 3; fast.k = 0.5 fits as 0; the FastK line follows row max(3, trunc(fast.k)) in all tables
CHECK bb16.12 FALSE HYPOTHESIS entry c is dirs row c: skipped iff the degree of row c equals the degree argument (holds in 439 of 970 steps)
CHECK bb16.13 TRUE entry c is slot c: skipped iff slot c is empty or its degree equals the degree argument (970 steps); D = degree + 1 (1774 of 1774), 102 if empty
CHECK bb16.14 TRUE the step line's Par is the parent's slot (343 of 343 interaction steps; read as a dirs row: 91)
CHECK bb16.15 FALSE HYPOTHESIS with fast.k = 0 every eligible term is searched every step (121 step-term cases of an eligible term in a slot above T, never visited)
CHECK bb16.16 TRUE fast.k = 0 visits every entry 1..T each step in table order, and gives the fit of fast.k = 1000
CHECK bb16.17 TRUE a searched entry gets K_m = K; skipped and unvisited entries keep K_m and RssDelta; entries T+1..T+a start at inf with K_m = K (905 of 905 steps)
CHECK bb16.18 TRUE the chosen parent is updated too: K_m = K and the largest RssDelta among the searched entries (905 of 905)
CHECK bb16.19 TRUE stored RssDelta = best legal trace-9 reduction (pairs, single hinges, linpreds terms; MaxG-0 knots excluded, 2 cases); 0 if none; -1 if no allowed pred (276 of 276)
CHECK bb16.20 TRUE MaxLegalRssDelta = min(1.01 * RssBeforeAddingHinge, 10 * previous chosen RssDelta) (49 of 49 steps), and MaxG 0 iff RssDelta is above it (15930 of 15930 knots)
CHECK bb16.21 TRUE the intercept is entry 1 in every table, but the window can leave it out (239 steps without it)
CHECK bb16.22 TRUE at degree 1 only the intercept is searched; fast.k = 3 ends the pass by reject (no DeltaRsq) at 5 terms (fast.k 20: 18)
CHECK bb16.23 TRUE a step that searches no entry adds nothing and ends the pass by reject (no DeltaRsq) (49 of 49); 16 more rejects searched only entries without a candidate
CHECK bb16.24 TRUE the only negative RssDelta is -1 (206 rows); 0 occurs in 891 rows
CHECK bb16.25 TRUE the Considering line lists the visited entries (970 of 970), but each bracket holds the RssDelta of the NEXT row (970 of 970); the last bracket of 433 lines lies past the table and is not checked
CHECK bb16.26 TRUE the defaults are fast.k = 20 and fast.beta = 1 (identical trace 6)
